{"table":"evidence","ref":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/evidence/concentration_source_warrant_pending","record":{"id":"concentration_source_warrant_pending","kind":"semantic_review","status":"not_run","command":[],"tool":"Authored consequence and inspected source; independent semantic acceptance not run","source_ids":["fggz2022_fixed_depth","qaoa_introduction"],"subject_ids":["circuit.fixed_word_concentration","circuit.one_measurement_near_optimum","qaoa_thermodynamic_first"],"details":"FGGZ §4 equations (13)–(14) give joint disorder/measurement first and second moments at a fixed word; equations (17)–(22) explain concentration. Choose the QAOA word at epsilon/2 accuracy before n and J. Markov applied to (Y_n-v_W)^2 bounds near-optimum failure by 4 epsilon^(-2) E[(Y_n-v_W)^2] -> 0. This uses a quantum second moment, not merely the square of the conditional mean. No rate, efficient angle search, uniform variable-depth theorem, every-instance guarantee or Lean result is asserted. Local source read: docs/annex/farhi-et-al-2022-qaoa-infinite-size.pdf, printed pages4–5; derived argument papers/qaoa-sk/long/reasoning-record.md §11.2."},"usage":{"record_ref":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/evidence/concentration_source_warrant_pending","paper_focus":[],"paper_memberships":[{"stage":"long","subgraph_ref":"sha256:7588abc48d1c21bb64c366849eaa851938d6acc6b17cf16f89ccf8b87ca26853/papers/long.json/support/0.3.1/69473417dc487cafa5e2e39b3168d2c4a8bffdad2e91b6e486de48f122dda071","roles":["associated_record"]},{"stage":"short","subgraph_ref":"sha256:b3fb22a55f09aba18f53cd9bbac859142355ee389bba5aa7bf98d016dc611a43/papers/short.json/support/0.3.1/77f0cf29ab577b42d8caa5b2831ebfb1ca170d4b13c1ef6897cadc8e93c2a834","roles":["associated_record"]},{"stage":"expository","subgraph_ref":"sha256:082c1187f897999ee934fa70dbb519221ed1e0aebc169fac91b7211a4a599dc5/papers/expository.json/support/0.3.1/9dd5536bc567fc55